# Port patch, a wish of the project owner (09.11.2026, from the OUYA branch's patch 0900; port/docs/whole-program-status.md,
# version 0.99.6, session B): the app menu's "View distance" (PERFORMANCE, Potato mode). cLightMgr::setFog and hokanMove
# give GX the fog runtime/view_distance.cpp returns for the room's LightEnv.Fog and set View's far plane to the one it
# returns (re4_view_fog: the fog's start and end scaled by the menu's level, the far plane from that end as the game
# computes it from the room's; rooms without fog, type 0, unchanged): what lies beyond the nearer fog is not drawn
# (scenery, figures, effects). Since 0.99.18 (wish of the project owner, 15.11.2026) re4_view_fog also makes the fog
# dense at a nearer far plane (the OUYA branch's patch 0901) and decides the level "Far" (since 1.0.0 the fog's end
# times 1.6, the far plane where that fog is 95 % dense; the project owner, 15.11.2026). LightEnv.Fog itself is not
# changed (the interpolation between two cuts reads it every frame). A new choice in the menu takes effect at once:
# hokanMove, which the light manager runs every frame, sets the fog again when the level changed and no interpolation
# runs (one that runs sets it itself). At "Normal": exactly as the game.
--- a/src/game/light.cpp
+++ b/src/game/light.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,10 @@
 #include "pendulum.h"
 #include "trans.h"

